:: Michael Ask for Nickname [nobr]

/* This is the scene that appears when the PC asks to be called by a nickname. */
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What’s up, dork?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> says, sticking his tongue out at you. You reply with a similarly juvenile insult, which causes him to chuckle. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Trust me, I know a lot more words I could call you, but that would just get me detention, which I don’t need right now. What’s up?”</span> You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> if he wouldn’t mind calling you by a nickname. Your real name is fine, and all, but since you are friends you’d rather if he called you by something else. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You mean besides dork? But it suits you so well!”</span> He laughs as you roll your eyes. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Fine! What does his royal dorkiness want to be called?”</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
<<textbox "$MichaelNickname" $MichaelNickname>><br>
<br>
	<<link "Continue">>
        <<replace "#choice">>
            <<set $Nickname.Michael to 1>>
            <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I don’t know, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$MichaelNickname</span> may be a little too cool for you.”</span> He sticks his tongue out once more, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Maybe I’ll just stick with dork?”</span> You cross your arms and glare at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span>, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Ugghh, fine! I’ll call you what you want! But you owe me!”</span> <br>
            <br>
            <<endByLocation>>
        <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>